      "explanation": "The doctor handled aspirin and ticagrelor safety very well, including no self-stopping, no double dosing, bleeding warnings, and prescriber follow-up. However, despite hyperlipidemia being visible and statin/lipid therapy being part of the authored cardiac medication-safety duty, the closure did not remind the family not to stop or omit statin/lipid therapy or to verify it on the final medication list; this is a minor/moderate omission, not a serious unsafe instruction.",
